Step 4 (Wave C): 8 context agents (17-24)

Tier mix: 17/21/24 = Sonnet; 18/20 = Haiku (deterministic-ish); 19/22/23 = Opus

agent-17 HTF Alignment (Sonnet, 500 tokens)
- Hard abstain when no HTF screenshot provided
- Does NOT re-derive HTF from macro cloud (Agent 02/08 own that)
- Score 0-14 = strong HTF disagreement (major downgrade signal)

agent-18 Time-of-Day Session (Haiku, 350 tokens)
- 14-bucket session lookup table (cash_open, mid_morning, lunch_chop,
  power_hour, globex_evening, asia_active, london, etc.)
- Multiplier in [0.7, 1.1] consumed by Wave E section 3
- Calibrated to general equity-index-futures consensus; needs
  empirical refit after 30-50 /NQ trades

agent-19 Comparable Historical Setup (Opus, 800 tokens) - THE SPINE
- Per Wave E spec section 1.3, abstain caps final composite at 60
- Receives top-K corpus candidates pre-retrieved by SQL kNN as text
  context (not separate images)
- Hard threshold cosine 0.62; abstain when below
- Reserves 1 of top-3 slots for high-similarity LOSER (per corpus
  README: "looked-textbook but failed" is highest-priority category)
- /NQ vs /ES instrument_caveat flag preserved with 0.92x penalty

agent-20 Setup Freshness (Haiku, 350 tokens, base composite contributor)
- Owns full setup_freshness factor (15% of Wave E composite)
- Count-based; Haiku-tractable
- Cascade discount: prior winners do NOT count as staleness (protects
  Image 05/11 multi-tap healthy trends)

agent-21 Market Internals (Sonnet, 500 tokens)
- VIX/ES/RTY/DXY/yields cross-asset correlation
- Hard abstain on single-symbol uploads
- Same-timeframe discipline; abstains within ±15 min FOMC
  (correlations broken)

agent-22 News & Event Risk (Opus, 600 tokens, VETO YES)
- 3-tier event taxonomy: T1 ±30min hard veto, T2 ±15min hard / ±60min
  downgrade, T3 mild penalty
- CPI/NFP open lockout: 9:30-10:00 ET auto-veto on release days
- Cluster rule: 2 T2 events within 60 min compound to T1-equivalent
- Powell live escalated to T1 (Q&A headline-parse risk)
- Optional event_context input for calendar override

agent-23 Behavioral State (Opus, 600 tokens, CONDITIONAL VETO)
- PRIVACY: never sees raw P&L. Categorical input only (session_color,
  trade counts, cadence flags, R-bucket counts) per Agent 37 spec
- Hard veto on confirmed_tilt + size_escalation OR cadence-after-loss
  <5min
- Soft veto on probable_tilt with chart-side <75
- 4hr break full reset; 60min break downgrades tilt one band
- Boredom-trading blind spot called out (Wave E composite check, not
  this single agent)
- Hard-veto override UX recommendation: 60s wait + typed reason

agent-24 Volatility Regime (Sonnet, 500 tokens)
- 5 regimes (DEAD/LOW/NORMAL/ELEVATED/EXTREME) with cloud-band
  thickness as primary vision-tractable signal (no exact ATR needed)
- Pattern × regime multiplier matrix; default Pullback column for V1
- DEAD forwards to Agent 25 (Disqualifier) as "no edge available"
- Backward-looking by construction; Agent 22 owns forward-event veto

Tests: 42 new tests across 8 agents covering enum exhaustiveness,
schema validation, abstain handling, optional-context-input wiring
(Agents 19/22/23 have additional input parameters), and tier/
max_tokens verification.

251 vitest passing total (208 from Wave B + 43 new). Pytest 134
unchanged. TypeScript type-check clean.
